                      01347         
                      01348         * Note: DAT is automatically available at power-up at
                      01349         * $F800.  However this goes away on the first write to
                      01350         * an odd address in the DAT. Therefore the first write
                      01351         * to the DAT must be to $F83E-$F83F to set up the monitor
                      01352         * in task 0. Then the monitor reset routine can finish
                      01353         * setting up the rest of task 0.
                      01354         
FFB4 8EF840           01355         RESETI  LDX    #DATRAM+64      reset DAT - map task 0 to
FFB7 CC01FF           01356                 LDD    #$1FF           bank 15, segment to block
FFBA ED83             01357         RES1    STD    ,--X           from the top down
FFBC 5A               01358                 DECB                   for the top 8K
FFBD 8CF838           01359                 CMPX   #DATRAM+56      ($E000-$FFFF)
FFC0 26F8             01360                 BNE    RES1
FFC2 8301E0           01361                 SUBD   #$1E0           map the rest of task 0
FFC5 ED83             01362         RES2    STD    ,--X           ($E000-$FFFF) to bank 15
FFC7 5A               01363                 DECB
FFC8 2AFB             01364                 BPL    RES2
FFCA 8EF82E           01365                 LDX    #COLD
FFCD BFE460           01366                 STX    >TRPVEC          set default ERRTRP value
FFD0 6E84             01367                 JMP    ,X             go to main GMXBUG coldstart
                      01368         
